From b87c1754a3711ac7a0c9dab339896a7b9aea42b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bhaskar Valaboju <bhaskar.valaboju@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 19:23:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] BACKPORT: tftp: ACK short DATA packets in WRQ window mode

This change is required in the Resolute tqftpserv package for proper
Wi-Fi functionality. Therefore, backport the change to Ubuntu Resolute,
which uses tqftpserv v1.1.1.

Link: https://github.com/linux-msm/tqftpserv/pull/37/
Signed-off-by: Bhaskar Valaboju <bhaskar.valaboju@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Pradeep P V K <pradeep.pragallapati@oss.qualcomm.com>
Origin: backport, https://github.com/linux-msm/tqftpserv/pull/37
Bug: https://github.com/linux-msm/tqftpserv/pull/37
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-04-22
---
 tqftpserv.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tqftpserv.c b/tqftpserv.c
index 9f7c15b..5d231aa 100644
--- a/tqftpserv.c
+++ b/tqftpserv.c
@@ -576,8 +576,9 @@ static int handle_writer(struct tftp_client *client)
 	memcpy(client->rw_buf + client->blk_offset, buf, payload);
 	client->blk_offset += payload;
 
-	/* Write to file if all the wsize blocks are recieved */
-	if (block % client->wsize == 0) {
+	/* Write to file if all the wsize blocks are recieved
+	 * or received buffer that is less than blksize */
+	if ((block % client->wsize == 0) || (payload < client->blksize)) {
 		ret = write(client->fd, client->rw_buf, client->blk_offset);
 		if (ret < 0) {
 			/* XXX: report error */
-- 
